WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.501
Ukrainian forces have lost

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.402
a significant amount

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.770
of troops and heavy equipment

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.437
in their assault

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.805
on Russian lines in the east.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.873
That is what a senior U.S.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.341
official is telling CNN.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.442
Two of them, actually.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.276
This is coming

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.212
just days after Ukraine's deputy

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.380
defense minister said

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.348
an offensive is taking place

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.083
in several directions.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:17.851
My next guest

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.686
is part of a bipartisan coalition

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.687
that just sent a letter

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.922
to President Biden, again urging the U.S.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.125
to provide Ukraine with fourth generation

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.159
fighter jets.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.660
That's a move that Russia says

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.596
would bring enormous risks.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:30.830
We're joined now by Congressman

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.531
Jason Crow.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.932
He is on the House Intelligence

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.401
and Foreign Affairs Committees.

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.102
He's also a former Army Ranger

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:36.703
who served three

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.872
combat tours in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.540
And he is now the co-chair

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.575
of the bipartisan four country caucus.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.643
A lot of stuff,

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.844
but I think all relevant to

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.579
what we're talking about here today,

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.647
this letter,

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.282
you're putting a lot of pressure

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.483
on the president.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.453
The president has softened on F-16's

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.020
a little bit.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.689
He has softened on these attack

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.858
arms, these longer range missile systems.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.127
So what do you want out of this?

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.395
Just for him to move faster?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.364
And what is the difference between him

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.398
going at the pace he's

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.666
going and going at the pace

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.534
you want him to?

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.568
Well, it's good to be with you.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.803
And I want to be really clear

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.703
that I think the president

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.538
and this administration

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:12.372
have done a remarkable

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.239
job of building

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.775
a coalition of over 50 countries,

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:17.911
most of whom have actually contributed

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.312
to the Ukrainian war effort,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.346
that is the world's

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.514
largest coalition

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.583
in support of a partner at war.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:24.717
We have

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.519
we have moved a massive amount

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.688
of arms, ammunition and equipment

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.890
We have trained multiple brigades

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.858
of the Ukrainian military.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.027
So this effort has been significant.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.296
But in war,

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.865
no day is like the last one days change,

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:39.699
weeks change.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.334
We have to evolve with the war effort.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.569
And what this letter is saying,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.938
this is a bipartisan effort

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.040
by the veteran's caucus in the House.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.141
We're coming out and saying

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.642
that you have the overwhelming

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:50.710
bipartisan support

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.112
of the House of Representatives,

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.880
the change, the nature of our support

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.648
to move certain things faster,

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.484
but also provide some longer range

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:58.751
strike capability

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.953
in the form of aircraft

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.354
and long range rockets

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.089
to help the Ukrainians win this.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.591
If they don't do that.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.425
On the timeline

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.259
that you're searching for,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.961
I mean, what's the risk

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:08.128
Well,

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:08.862
the risk is,

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.096
is that the Ukrainians

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.232
have a series of wins and battles,

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.400
but they could lose the longer term war.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.401
The timelines here

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.769
are different, Brianna,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:17.971
but Vladimir Putin is playing

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:18.938
a long game.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.240
He's looking one year,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.674
two years, three years out.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.076
He thinks that the West

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.511
and Democratic nations

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.778
will lose interest,

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.312
that we can't

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.947
sustain the political support.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.315
And he can just grind this out.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.617
He's willing to send

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.285
100,000 200,000

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.653
Russians to their death

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.087
in hopes

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.256
that he can win this in the long term.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.490
So what we have to do is help

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.024
the Ukrainians

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.026
win this in the short or mid-term.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:40.460
Help them

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.095
destroy the Russian military

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.596
and their capacity to wage war.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.632
Now, let's talk about the longer term

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.332
of supplying

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.635
something like F-16s to the Ukrainians.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.470
They need logistical support.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.105
They need maintenance on that. Right.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.841
These are finely tuned machines.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.277
How would Ukraine get that

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.812
if they get F-16s from the U.S.?

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:00.213
Well, that's

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.881
what our letter calls for, is

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.849
an expedited

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:03.917
all of government,

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.385
all of alliance effort

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.853
to train the pilots,

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.955
find the F-16s and transfer them

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.257
either directly from the United States

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.826
or a transfer from one of our allies,

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.028
as there's F-16s

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.429
throughout the NATO's alliance

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.931
in several countries,

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.498
might be able

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:18.965
to transfer

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.533
them much quicker than we could,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.368
but also train the maintainers

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.903
These are sophisticated aircraft.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.238
That's why they're so good

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.340
They require a tremendous amount of back

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.342
end support and sustainment.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.843
So we're going to train the mechanics.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:31.477
We're going to have to get

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.946
the fuel supplies going.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.913
There's a lot of things

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.448
that have to happen now

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.483
so that six months, nine months from now,

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.851
these aircraft can be flying over

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.986
Ukrainian skies.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.920
And that's what we're pushing

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.988
the administration to do.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.456
The Russian foreign minister,

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.959
Sergey Lavrov, said F-16s

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.328
could accommodate nuclear weapons.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.196
He's clearly sending a message here.

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.265
What is he really saying is you see it?

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.300
And does that dissuade you at all

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.168
from pushing for this?

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.736
Well, first of all, this administration

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.570
and President Biden

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.972
have been very careful

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.907
of making sure that we are

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.575
we are not escalating,

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.743
that we're not doing anything

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.445
that would give them a reason

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.480
to do a catastrophic action

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.248
like nuclear weapons,

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.582
unconventional weapons.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.550
We've been very cautious

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.619
and deliberate every step of the way.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.520
But another really important

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:14.988
point is

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:17.190
we should never allow dictators

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.192
and rogue nations

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.927
to dictate the terms

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:21.261
of what

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:21.928
we're willing to do

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:23.229
to defend our partners

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.030
every time

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.832
Putin or Lavrov has established

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.899
some kind of red line.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.602
We have

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.371
done things to support Ukraine,

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.505
and they haven't

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:33.573
escalated from that point.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.808
So we should not give Vladimir Putin

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.909
or anybody else, for that matter,

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.244
a veto authority over

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.045
what we're willing to do

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.113
to stand by our friends.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:40.847
These attack them.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.315
So these are the longer range missiles

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.850
that would dramatically increase

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:44.851
Ukraine's capability.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.451
We're talking about

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:48.321
going to almost 200 miles distance.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:48.921
Right.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.991
There was concern before the White House

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.660
softened on this a little bit about

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.129
this could take the U.S.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.163
into World War Three.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.032
You would be giving the capability

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.867
to the Ukrainians of going

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.302
well into Russia.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.803
How do you get assurances?

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:04.570
How do you ensure

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.571
that they don't do that?

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:06.773
I just don't buy that

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.708
because we have seen now 16

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.443
months into that this war

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:13.112
of Zelensky

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:13.279
and the

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:15.782
Ukrainians have shown their capability

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.417
to actually be a good partner.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.151
They are not going to

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:20.320
jeopardize aid from the United States

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.622
by misusing our aid.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.090
We have asked for assurances

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.858
that they're not going to use our weapons

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.860
and our technology to strike into Russia.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.796
They have kept those assurances.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.030
They have kept those promises,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.131
and there's absolutely no reason

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:32.498
to believe

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.733
that they're going to break that promise

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:34.467
because it's

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.069
not in their interest to do so.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.203
So they're going to do

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.204
what they need to do to win.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.872
They'll use their own technology

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.707
to do cross-border

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:42.875
strikes, their own weapons and equipment

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.310
but they're not going to use U.S.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.111
aid to do that.

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.412
And I don't think we have any reason

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.347
to believe that they would.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.247
All right. We'll follow this.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.582
We'll see what the reaction is from

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.083
the White House

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:50.850
to this request

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.051
that this bipartisan group,

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.453
including yourself, were making

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:54.387
Congressman Jason Crow.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.555
Thanks for your time. Good to be on.

